=== cost of the whole lattice-dynamics workflow per model (force calls) ===
  MACE-MP-0 small  61 calls (9 EOS of 5 atoms, 9 phonon supercells, 22 tilt points, 16 relaxation steps, 5 timing), total CPU 50 s
  CHGNet 0.3.0     58 calls (9 EOS of 5 atoms, 9 phonon supercells, 22 tilt points, 13 relaxation steps, 5 timing), total CPU 40 s
  SevenNet-0       55 calls (9 EOS of 5 atoms, 9 phonon supercells, 22 tilt points, 10 relaxation steps, 5 timing), total CPU 47 s
  MatterSim 1M     56 calls (9 EOS of 5 atoms, 9 phonon supercells, 22 tilt points, 11 relaxation steps, 5 timing), total CPU 26 s

=== two routes to the R4+ curvature: frozen tilt profile E(u) versus phonopy forces ===
  fit E = c2 u^2 + c4 u^4 per f.u. for tilt <= 6 deg (u = equatorial O displacement, two O per f.u. move),
  then omega^2 = c2 / m_O ;  1 sqrt(eV/(A^2 amu)) = 521.47 cm-1
  MACE-MP-0 small  c2 = -0.293 eV/A^2, c4 = 6.16 eV/A^4 ->  71i cm-1 ; phonopy R4+ (0.01 A)  71i cm-1
  CHGNet 0.3.0     c2 = -0.129 eV/A^2, c4 = 4.40 eV/A^4 ->  47i cm-1 ; phonopy R4+ (0.01 A)  22i cm-1
  SevenNet-0       c2 = -0.254 eV/A^2, c4 = 5.42 eV/A^4 ->  66i cm-1 ; phonopy R4+ (0.01 A)  65i cm-1
  MatterSim 1M     c2 = -0.222 eV/A^2, c4 = 5.97 eV/A^4 ->  61i cm-1 ; phonopy R4+ (0.01 A)  63i cm-1
